 "readme": {
  "file": "README.md",
  "title": "Certifying the Riemann hypothesis up to bounded height in Lean",
  "excerpt": "This repository proves in Lean's kernel that all the nontrivial zeros of the Riemann zeta function up to a specified height $T$ lie on the critical line, as predicted by the Riemann hypothesis. Intervals are certified on the critical line, proving the location of nontrivial zeros with configurable precision. The main theorem is proved fully in the kernel, depending only on the standard axiom set `[propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]`."
 },
